{%- comment -%}
  PG R36S Mobile: one swipeable gallery, the orb page's running order, and an
  ADD TO CART inside every offer tile.

  Registered in templates/product.pg-landing.json only (the R36S). Every visual
  rule is ≤900px — desktop keeps the gallery and the column it has today.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- THE GALLERY

  pg-landing renders three separate things: .pgx-hero (the first image),
  .pgx-vid (the clip from the section's "Gallery video URL" setting) and
  .pgx-thumbwrap (every other image). On a phone that reads as one big photo,
  then a video, then a wall of pictures.

  On phones they are now ONE carousel, like the orb: the strip is the gallery,
  one item fills the view, and a "‹ SWIPE · n/N ›" pill on the photo says how
  far along you are. Nothing is dropped — the hero photo is copied in as the
  first slide, the video is MOVED in as the second, and the rest follow in
  their product order.

  Copied, not moved, for the hero: pg-landing's own thumbnail clicks write to
  #pgx-hero-img, so moving that node into the strip would give the shopper a
  slide whose picture changes under them. A copy takes the hero's src once, at
  build time, and then stands still. The hero container is hidden only once the
  copy is in place (the html.pg-r36-gal class), so a failure leaves the page
  looking exactly as it does today rather than with no photo at all.

  The video IS moved, since a second <video> would download the clip twice, and
  it leaves a placeholder behind so rotating past 900px puts it back where
  pg-landing had it. The desktop DOM is restored on that same pass.

  The pill is pg-gallery-tweaks' markup and styling restated: that file is
  registered on the orb template only, so the class names cannot collide here,
  and repeating them is what makes the two pages look identical. The counter
  repaints on every animation frame while the strip scrolls, not on a debounce,
  so it counts up under the finger instead of jumping when the strip settles.

  ------------------------------------------------------------ THE BUY COLUMN

  The orb's phone layout comes from pg-tiktok-pdp, which turns .pgx-buy into a
  flex column and gives each child an explicit order. The R36S had pg-landing's
  plain DOM order — the review carousel directly under the stars, above the
  bundle. The same order values are restated so both pages read:

      title | stars | BUNDLE & SAVE | tiles | add to cart | sellout risk
      | review carousel | info row | payment | guarantee | accordions

  Order, not DOM moves: pg-mobile's quoteUp() re-seats the review card after the
  rating every 1.5s and would fight a relocation. pg-sellout-last (also on this
  template) is what puts the sellout card under the last tile; this file only
  gives its wrapper the seat.

  --------------------------------------------------- AN ADD TO CART PER TILE

  Like the orb, where pg-tiktok-pdp puts one in every ladder tile: visible only
  in the selected tile, with the big bottom button hidden on phones so exactly
  one button is on screen and it belongs to the offer being looked at.

  It must cover BOTH of this page's tiles, which come from different places and
  share only .pgx-tile: the Single Item tile is pg-landing's own, and the Duo
  Pack is built by pgDuo (pg-theme-css) as `.pgx-tile.pgx-duo`. An earlier pass
  keyed on pg-landing's [data-pgx-tile] attribute and so skipped the Duo Pack
  entirely — the selector here is every .pgx-tile in the buy column.

  A click clicks #pgx-atc, and each tile's own owner takes it from there:
  pgDuo listens for a .pgx-atc click in the CAPTURE phase and, while its tile is
  selected, posts the two chosen versions and stops the event, so pg-landing's
  handler does not also fire; with the single tile selected pgDuo bows out and
  pg-landing's handler posts the single variant. A programmatic .click() reaches
  both even though the bottom button is display:none, which is what lets it be
  hidden while still doing the work. The button is a SPAN with role=button (the
  base theme paints real buttons with a dark ::before overlay) and deliberately
  does NOT carry .pgx-atc, or pgDuo's handler would fire from the in-tile button
  itself and double-post. It only appears in the selected tile, so by the time
  it can be pressed the tile it belongs to is already the one that will be sold.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* off at every width except phones, where the rules below turn them on */
  #pgx .pg-gt-swipe{display:none}
  #pgx .pgx-tile .pg-r36-atc{display:none}

  @media (max-width:900px){
    /* ---- one carousel: hero copy, then the clip, then every other photo ---- */
    html.pg-r36-gal #pgx .pgx-hero{display:none !important}
    #pgx .pgx-thumbwrap{display:block !important;position:relative !important;margin-top:0 !important}
    #pgx .pgx-thumbwrap .pgx-thumbs{
      display:flex !important;flex-wrap:nowrap !important;
      overflow-x:auto !important;scroll-behavior:smooth;
      scroll-snap-type:x mandatory;
      gap:10px !important;margin-top:0 !important;
      scrollbar-width:none;-ms-overflow-style:none;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;
    }
    #pgx .pgx-thumbwrap .pgx-thumbs::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
    #pgx .pgx-thumbwrap .pgx-thumbs > *{flex:0 0 100% !important;scroll-snap-align:center}
    #pgx .pgx-thumbwrap .pgx-thumbs button{padding:0;border:0;background:#0D0714;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;cursor:pointer}
    #pgx .pgx-thumbwrap .pgx-thumbs button img{aspect-ratio:1/1 !important;object-fit:cover !important;width:100% !important;height:auto !important}
    #pgx .pgx-thumbwrap .pgx-thumbs .pgx-vid{margin:0 !important;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;background:#0d0d0d}
    #pgx .pgx-thumbwrap .pgx-thumbs .pgx-vid video{
      width:100% !important;display:block;
      aspect-ratio:1/1 !important;object-fit:cover !important;
      height:auto !important;max-height:none !important;
    }
    /* phones swipe; the arrows sat on top of the picture */
    #pgx .pgx-tharrow{display:none !important}

    /* ---- the swipe pill, as on the orb ---- */
    #pgx .pgx-thumbwrap .pg-gt-swipe{
      display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:10px;
      position:absolute;bottom:10px;top:auto;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);
      z-index:4;margin:0;padding:11px 20px;
      width:max-content;max-width:100%;
      border-radius:999px;
      background:rgba(11,7,16,.82);
      border:1px solid rgba(190,140,235,.55);
      box-shadow:0 6px 18px -6px rgba(0,0,0,.8);
      color:#EEE1FB;
      font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
      font-size:15px;font-weight:800;
      letter-spacing:.10em;text-transform:uppercase;
      white-space:nowrap;pointer-events:none;
    }
    #pgx .pg-gt-swipe span{display:inline-block;font-size:23px;line-height:.7;color:#F6ECFF;animation:pgGtNudge 1.5s ease-in-out infinite}
    #pgx .pg-gt-swipe .pg-gt-l{animation-direction:reverse}
    /* fixed width, so the centred pill does not shimmy as the digits change */
    #pgx .pg-gt-swipe b.pg-gt-n{
      display:inline-block;min-width:4.8ch;text-align:center;
      font-weight:800;color:#FFFFFF;letter-spacing:.04em;
      font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;
    }

    /* ---- the orb page's running order ---- */
    #pgx .pgx-buy{display:flex;flex-direction:column}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > *{order:7}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-title{order:1}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-rating{order:2}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-bs{order:3}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-divider{order:3}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-tile{order:4}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-deal-note{order:5}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-atc{order:5}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-err{order:6}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-quote{order:8;margin-top:16px}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-sellout{order:9}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-info{order:10}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pg-payrow{order:11}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-pay{order:11}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-guar{order:12}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-acc{order:13}

    /* ---- an ADD TO CART inside the selected tile ---- */
    #pgx .pgx-tile.pgx-sel .pg-r36-atc{
      display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;
      margin-top:12px;padding:15px 12px;
      border-radius:10px;
      background:linear-gradient(120deg,#9B4BC4 0%,#7A2FA2 55%,#5E2380 100%);
      color:#FFFFFF;
      font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
      font-size:15.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;
      text-align:center;cursor:pointer;
      box-shadow:0 14px 30px -12px rgba(139,68,190,.75);
      -webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;
      transition:filter .15s ease,opacity .15s ease;
    }
    #pgx .pgx-tile.pgx-sel .pg-r36-atc:hover{filter:brightness(1.1)}
    #pgx .pgx-tile.pgx-sel .pg-r36-atc.busy{opacity:.6;cursor:default}
    #pgx .pgx-tile.pgx-sel .pg-r36-atc:after{content:"\2192";font-size:17px;line-height:1}
    /* the bottom button duplicates the in-tile one on phones. Browsers without
       :has() simply keep both, which is harmless. */
    #pgx .pgx-buy:has(.pgx-tile .pg-r36-atc) > .pgx-atc{display:none !important}
  }

  @keyframes pgGtNudge{
    0%,100%{transform:translateX(0);opacity:.55}
    50%    {transform:translateX(4px);opacity:1}
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
    #pgx .pg-gt-swipe span{animation:none}
  }
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgR36Mobile) return; window.pgR36Mobile = 1;

  function mobile(){ return !window.matchMedia || window.matchMedia('(max-width: 900px)').matches; }

  /* ---------------- the carousel ---------------- */

  var HEROSRC = '';   /* read once: thumbnail clicks rewrite #pgx-hero-img */

  function gallery(){
    var wrap = document.querySelector('#pgx .pgx-thumbwrap');
    if (!wrap) return;
    var strip = wrap.querySelector('.pgx-thumbs');
    if (!strip) return;

    if (mobile()){
      var hero = document.getElementById('pgx-hero-img');
      if (hero && !HEROSRC) HEROSRC = hero.getAttribute('src') || '';
      if (HEROSRC && !strip.querySelector('.pg-r36-slide')){
        var b = document.createElement('button');
        b.type = 'button';
        b.className = 'pg-r36-slide';
        var im = document.createElement('img');
        im.src = HEROSRC;
        im.alt = (hero && hero.getAttribute('alt')) || '';
        b.appendChild(im);
        strip.insertBefore(b, strip.firstChild);
      }
      /* the clip becomes the second slide, leaving a marker in its old seat */
      var vid = document.querySelector('#pgx .pgx-vid');
      if (vid && vid.parentNode !== strip){
        if (!vid.pgR36Ph){
          var ph = document.createElement('i');
          ph.className = 'pg-r36-ph';
          ph.hidden = true;
          vid.parentNode.insertBefore(ph, vid);
          vid.pgR36Ph = ph;
        }
        var lead = strip.querySelector('.pg-r36-slide');
        strip.insertBefore(vid, lead ? lead.nextSibling : strip.firstChild);
      }
      if (strip.querySelector('.pg-r36-slide')) document.documentElement.classList.add('pg-r36-gal');
      pill(wrap, strip);
    } else {
      /* rotated back to desktop: put pg-landing's gallery back as it was */
      var v2 = strip.querySelector('.pgx-vid');
      if (v2 && v2.pgR36Ph && v2.pgR36Ph.parentNode){
        v2.pgR36Ph.parentNode.insertBefore(v2, v2.pgR36Ph);
        v2.pgR36Ph.parentNode.removeChild(v2.pgR36Ph);
        v2.pgR36Ph = null;
      }
      var s2 = strip.querySelector('.pg-r36-slide');
      if (s2 && s2.parentNode) s2.parentNode.removeChild(s2);
      document.documentElement.classList.remove('pg-r36-gal');
    }
  }

  function pill(wrap, strip){
    var el = wrap.querySelector('.pg-gt-swipe');
    if (!el){
      if (strip.children.length < 2) return;      /* nothing to swipe to */
      el = document.createElement('div');
      el.className = 'pg-gt-swipe';
      el.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
      el.innerHTML = '<span class="pg-gt-l">&lsaquo;</span> Swipe &middot; <b class="pg-gt-n"></b> <span>&rsaquo;</span>';
      wrap.appendChild(el);
    }
    paint();
  }

  /* which slide is in view. Synchronous and allocation-light: safe to call once
     per animation frame while the strip is being swiped. */
  function paint(){
    var wrap = document.querySelector('#pgx .pgx-thumbwrap');
    if (!wrap) return;
    var strip = wrap.querySelector('.pgx-thumbs');
    var cnt = wrap.querySelector('.pg-gt-swipe .pg-gt-n');
    if (!strip || !cnt) return;
    var kids = strip.children;
    if (!kids.length) return;
    var mid = strip.scrollLeft + strip.clientWidth / 2;
    var best = 0, bestD = Infinity;
    for (var i = 0; i < kids.length; i++){
      var k = kids[i];
      var d = Math.abs((k.offsetLeft + k.offsetWidth / 2) - mid);
      if (d < bestD){ bestD = d; best = i; }
    }
    var pos = (best + 1) + '/' + kids.length;
    if (cnt.textContent !== pos) cnt.textContent = pos;
  }

  /* ---------------- an ADD TO CART in every tile ---------------- */

  function buttons(){
    /* every tile in the buy column: pg-landing's Single Item AND pgDuo's
       Duo Pack, which share only .pgx-tile */
    document.querySelectorAll('#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-tile').forEach(function(tile){
      if (tile.querySelector('.pg-r36-atc')) return;
      var b = document.createElement('span');
      b.className = 'pg-r36-atc';
      b.setAttribute('role', 'button');
      b.setAttribute('tabindex', '0');
      b.textContent = 'Add to cart';
      b.addEventListener('click', function(){
        if (b.classList.contains('busy')) return;
        var atc = document.getElementById('pgx-atc');
        if (!atc) return;
        b.classList.add('busy');
        b.textContent = 'Adding…';
        /* whichever tile is selected owns the click: pgDuo intercepts it in the
           capture phase for the Duo Pack, pg-landing's own handler posts the
           single variant otherwise */
        atc.click();
        setTimeout(function(){ b.classList.remove('busy'); b.textContent = 'Add to cart'; }, 2600);
      });
      b.addEventListener('keydown', function(e){
        if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' '){ e.preventDefault(); b.click(); }
      });
      tile.appendChild(b);
    });
  }

  function pass(){ gallery(); buttons(); }

  function boot(){
    pass();
    /* the strip's own scrolling: `scroll` does not bubble but it does capture,
       and listening on the document survives the gallery being rebuilt */
    var raf = 0;
    document.addEventListener('scroll', function(e){
      var t = e.target;
      if (!t || !t.classList || !t.classList.contains('pgx-thumbs')) return;
      if (!raf) raf = requestAnimationFrame(function(){ raf = 0; paint(); });
    }, {capture: true, passive: true});

    var root = document.getElementById('pgx');
    if (root && window.MutationObserver){
      var q = false;
      /* pgDuo rebuilds its tile on an interval, and the gallery can be
         re-rendered under us; every pass is idempotent */
      new MutationObserver(function(){
        if (q) return;
        q = true;
        setTimeout(function(){ q = false; pass(); }, 80);
      }).observe(root, {childList: true, subtree: true});
    }
    window.addEventListener('resize', function(){ pass(); paint(); }, {passive: true});
    setInterval(pass, 900);
    [300, 900, 2000, 4000].forEach(function(t){ setTimeout(function(){ pass(); paint(); }, t); });
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot); else boot();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG R36S Mobile", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG R36S Mobile"}]}
{% endschema %}
